Subject: [PATCH] gralloc: do not ask for the camera ION heap

0x00400000 is GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_CAMERA_HEAP to this gralloc and, since Android 8,
BufferUsage::VIDEO_DECODER to the framework, which sets it on the output buffers of a
hardware video decoder. This tablet's kernel has no camera ION heap (the heaps are
audio, mm, qsecom and system), so every such allocation failed: "ION_IOC_ALLOC failed
with error - No such device", heap 0x100000, and the decoder stopped before its first
frame. That is how VP9 video in the browser stayed still with no sound.

With no camera heap in the kernel, asking for it can only fail. So the bit no longer
selects a heap, and the buffer comes from the heaps the other bits name, or from the
system heap.

diff --git a/libgralloc/alloc_controller.cpp b/libgralloc/alloc_controller.cpp
--- a/libgralloc/alloc_controller.cpp
+++ b/libgralloc/alloc_controller.cpp
@@ -448,8 +448,9 @@
         ionHeapId |= ION_HEAP(ION_SYSTEM_HEAP_ID);
     }
 
-    if(usage & GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_CAMERA_HEAP)
-        ionHeapId |= ION_HEAP(ION_CAMERA_HEAP_ID);
+    // GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_CAMERA_HEAP is BufferUsage::VIDEO_DECODER to the
+    // framework, and the kernel has no camera heap: it no longer selects one.
+    // tools/tree-patches/hardware/qcom-caf/msm8952/display/0001 says more.
 
     if(usage & GRALLOC_USAGE_PRIVATE_ADSP_HEAP)
         ionHeapId |= ION_HEAP(ION_ADSP_HEAP_ID);
